------ Deferred from the master role + custom-report upload feature ------
SECURITY: custom-report uploads are unsandboxed arbitrary code execution
  app/routes/master.py's upload_custom_report saves straight to
  custom_report_path() after only a compile() syntax check (catches typos, not
  malice) and a master-role gate. custom_report_loader.load_custom_module()
  exec's the file server-side on every report generation for that school.
  Accepted for now because provisioning master accounts is already a trusted,
  CLI-only action -- but if that ever changes, this needs real sandboxing
  (subprocess isolation, restricted exec environment) before it's safe.

